.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo

.env

data/
starter/data
workspace/
*.tar.gz
*.parquet
*.feather

*.model
*.pkl
*.joblib
*.txt.bak

# Run bulk, matched whatever a run directory is called. The original patterns
# assumed runs/<id>/..., so a sibling directory like runs-alice/ slipped past them
# and would have committed 2.4 MB checkpoints and 4.4 MB submissions. These are
# deliberately name-agnostic: several people generating runs should not each have
# to remember the convention.
**/checkpoints/
**/submission.csv
runs*/**/best/
runs*/*/best/

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Unfiltered organiser stdout. Contains hidden-test metrics by construction.
# Human-only. Never commit, never read into a prompt or a machine-readable log.
runs/raw_starter_output/
runs/quarantine/
runs/review/

# Generated model code, live only while an experiment is running. The ledger
# archives each patch to runs/<id>/patches/ when it finishes, and that copy is
# the one worth keeping.
harness/models/gen/*.py
harness/features/gen/*.py

# Intermediate submissions: 4.4 MB each and regenerable in minutes. The ONE
# submission that is actually submitted is added explicitly with `git add -f`,
# so there is never ambiguity about which file was scored.

# Local screenshots and scratch images
image.png
*.screenshot.png

# Screenshots and images dropped at the repo root for review. These are working
# material, not deliverables, and a `git add -A` swept three of them into a commit
# once. Images that belong in the repo live under docs/ and are added explicitly.
/*.png
/*.jpg
/*.jpeg
/*.gif

# Presentation working material. Kept locally, never committed.
/script.txt
/devpost_story.docx
/devpost_story.md
/submission_bundle.zip
